docs {
  # POST /api/v1/search/auto

  **Auto search** — `route_query` (small tier) classifies the question,
  then dispatches to local / global / drift as a child workflow.
  Fail-safe: a flaky/ambiguous router defaults to **local**, so auto
  never breaks.

  ## When to use
  You don't know the mode up front / mixed traffic / programmatic
  clients that can't classify. Costs one extra small-LLM call for the
  routing decision.

  ## Request body
  - **query** *(required)*. **top_k** *(default 10)*.

  ## Response 200 — `SearchResponse`; `mode` is set to the **chosen**
  route (`local` | `global` | `drift`).

  ## Errors
  - `401` — auth. `500` — workflow raised.
}
